Negative control for the picker opening on a real SURFACE (`R7-3`).

Puts the ui menu panel back on shadcn's `bg-popover` / `text-popover-foreground`,
which this theme defines nowhere — so the panel keeps its portal, its ring, its
position and its behaviour, and paints no fill at all. The table rows and the
status badges under it read straight through the menu, which is exactly what the
operator was shown.

The control is on the ui panel rather than on the picker deliberately: the
picker composes the package's menu, so a picker that renders opaque only because
it restated some background of its own would leave every other menu in the
product transparent.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-picker spec's panel case — the opened menu no longer carries
the theme's own surface and elevation.

